IMPORT prelude

-- Prevention of Pollution of the Sea Act 1990 (Singapore) -- the meaning of "oily mixture" (s 2(1)), oil discharged from land or a
-- transfer apparatus and its special defences (ss 3, 4), throwing pollutants into Singapore waters (s 5), discharges from ships of
-- garbage and the like, oil, noxious liquid substances, and ballast water and sediments, with their exceptions and defences (ss 6, 7,
-- 10, 10A, 10B), who answers for a ship's discharge (s 2(1) "master"), the duty to report a ship's discharge (s 15), the ship
-- owner's liability for removal costs (ss 17, 18), the government-ship exemption (s 26(1)), selected penalties (ss 3, 5, 7, 8,
-- 14(3), 15, 22(3), 24(1)), the continuing fine for ignoring a reception-facility direction (s 11(6)) and composition (s 33).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PPSA1990.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; its metadata calls it the current
-- version as at 1 October 2026. The latest amendment annotated in the text is Act 26 of 2017 (Prevention of Pollution of the Sea
-- (Amendment) Act 2017, in force 8 September 2017, per the Legislative History).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0110 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. A person meets this Act by tipping rubbish off a jetty or a boat (s 5); a business meets it by running a shipyard,
-- refinery or bunkering barge on the shore (ss 3, 4, 16), or by owning, managing or acting as agent for a ship that calls in
-- Singapore (ss 6 to 10B, 15, 17, 18).
--
-- Not encoded: sediments from land or an apparatus (s 5A), s 8's elements (only its penalty), the notification duty for
-- noxious liquid cargoes (s 9), reception facilities beyond s 11(6), the record-book regulations and evidence (ss 12 to 14 beyond
-- the s 14(3) penalty), the land-side reporting duty (s 16, comment only), removal costs from land and from persons (ss 19 to 21,
-- comment only), inspectors, detention, sale, arrest and the other Part 6 machinery (ss 22 to 32 beyond the penalties), the
-- Minister's discretionary exemptions (s 26(2), (3)) and the regulations (s 34). No regulations were retrieved, so what is
-- "prescribed" -- the reporting circumstances, the compoundable offences, the ballast water management standard, the substances
-- listed as noxious -- is unknown here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Prevention of Pollution of the Sea Act 1990 -- discharges`

DECLARE Pollutant IS ONE OF
    `oil`
    `an oily mixture`
    `refuse`
    `garbage`
    `plastics`
    `waste matter`
    `a carcase`
    `a noxious liquid substance`
    `a marine pollutant in packaged form`
    `trade effluent`
    `sediments`
    `ballast water`
    `sewage`

§§ `2(1) -- oily mixture`

-- s 2(1): "oily mixture" means "a mixture with an oil content of 15 parts or more in 1 million parts of the mixture".
GIVEN `oil parts per million` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mixture is an oily mixture` IF
    `oil parts per million` AT LEAST 15

§§ `3 and 4 -- oil from land or a transfer apparatus`

-- s 3: if oil or an oily mixture is discharged into Singapore waters "from any place on land, or from any apparatus used for
-- transferring oil from or to any ship" -- (a) from a place on land, "the occupier of that place or if the discharge is caused by the
-- act of another person who is in that place without the permission (express or implied) of the occupier, that person"; (b) from an
-- apparatus, "the person in charge of the apparatus" -- is guilty of an offence: a fine "of not less than $1,000 and not more than
-- $1 million" or imprisonment up to 2 years or both.
-- s 4(1): a defence for the occupier or the person in charge "to prove that the discharge ... was not due to any want of reasonable
-- care, and that as soon as practicable after the discharge was discovered all reasonable steps were taken for stopping or reducing
-- it". (2): a defence for the occupier "to prove that the discharge was caused by the act of a person who was in that place without
-- the permission (express or implied) of the occupier". (3): for an oily mixture from a place on land, a defence to prove (a) the oil
-- "was contained in an effluent produced by operations for the refining of oil", (b) "it was not reasonably practicable to dispose of
-- the effluent otherwise than by discharging it into Singapore waters", and (c) "all reasonably practicable steps had been taken for
-- eliminating oil from the effluent". (4): if the waters or adjacent land were "fouled by oil", (3) does not apply "unless the court
-- is satisfied that the fouling was not caused, or contributed to, by oil contained in any effluent discharged at or before that time
-- from that place".
--
-- s 3(a) names the trespasser in place of the occupier, yet s 4(2) gives the occupier a defence for the trespasser's act. The
-- encoding follows s 3(a) for who is liable and keeps s 4(2) as a defence for an occupier who is charged anyway.
DECLARE `Section 3 party` IS ONE OF
    `the occupier`
    `the person there without permission`
    `the person in charge of the apparatus`

GIVEN `came from a place on land` IS A BOOLEAN, `caused by a person there without permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Section 3 party`
`the person liable under section 3` MEANS
    IF NOT `came from a place on land` THEN `the person in charge of the apparatus`
    ELSE IF `caused by a person there without permission` THEN `the person there without permission`
         ELSE `the occupier`

DECLARE `Land discharge` HAS
    `from a place on land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an oily mixture rather than oil` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by a trespasser` IS A BOOLEAN
    `not due to want of reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all reasonable steps taken to stop or reduce it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `oil was in refinery effluent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no practicable alternative to discharging into Singapore waters` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all practicable steps taken to eliminate the oil` IS A BOOLEAN
    `waters or adjacent land fouled by oil` IS A BOOLEAN
    `court satisfied the fouling was not from that place's effluent` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the discharge` IS A `Land discharge`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 4 defence is made out` IF
        (`the discharge`'s `not due to want of reasonable care` AND `the discharge`'s `all reasonable steps taken to stop or reduce it`)
    OR  (`the discharge`'s `from a place on land` AND `the discharge`'s `caused by a trespasser`)
    OR  (    `the discharge`'s `from a place on land`
         AND `the discharge`'s `is an oily mixture rather than oil`
         AND `the discharge`'s `oil was in refinery effluent`
         AND `the discharge`'s `no practicable alternative to discharging into Singapore waters`
         AND `the discharge`'s `all practicable steps taken to eliminate the oil`
         AND ((NOT `the discharge`'s `waters or adjacent land fouled by oil`)
              OR `the discharge`'s `court satisfied the fouling was not from that place's effluent`))

§§ `5 -- throwing pollutants into Singapore waters`

-- s 5: "Any person who puts, throws, casts or deposits into Singapore waters, or causes to be put, thrown, cast or deposited
-- thereinto, any oil, oily mixture, refuse, garbage, plastics, waste matter, carcase, noxious liquid substances, marine pollutant in
-- packaged form or trade effluent" -- a fine up to $20,000 or imprisonment up to 6 months or both. Sediments, ballast water and
-- sewage are not in the list (sediments from land have their own offence in s 5A).
GIVEN `the pollutant` IS A Pollutant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5 forbids putting it into Singapore waters` IF
    CONSIDER `the pollutant`
    WHEN `sediments` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `ballast water` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `sewage` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `6, 7, 10, 10A, 10B and 26(1) -- discharges from ships`

-- s 6(1): a discharge of "refuse, garbage, waste matter, trade effluent, plastics or marine pollutant in packaged form ... from any
-- ship into Singapore waters". (2) not where (a) "necessary for the purpose of securing the safety of a ship or saving life at sea",
-- or (b) it escaped "in consequence of damage, other than intentional damage, to the ship or its equipment, and all reasonable
-- precautions were taken after the occurrence of the damage or the discovery of the discharge". (3) not where "a synthetic fishing
-- net ... is lost at sea, and all reasonable precautions were taken to prevent the loss". (4) damage is intentional if the master,
-- owner or agent "acted with intent to cause the damage" or "acted recklessly and with knowledge that damage would probably result".
-- s 7(1): oil or oily mixture "from a Singapore ship into any part of the sea or from any ship into Singapore waters". (2)(a), (b) as
-- s 6, and (c) "in the case of an oily mixture", a discharge "for the purpose of combating specific pollution incidents ... approved
-- by the appointed authority".
-- s 10(1): a noxious liquid substance or mixture "carried as cargo or part cargo in bulk", from a Singapore ship into the sea or any
-- ship into Singapore waters. (2)(a) to (c) as s 7, but (c) is not confined to mixtures.
-- s 10A(1): ballast water or sediments from any ship into Singapore waters or from a Singapore ship into any part of the sea; (2) not
-- "through ballast water management in accordance with regulations made under section 34". s 10B: a defence "to prove, on a balance
-- of probabilities", that (a) it was necessary for the safety of the ship "in an emergency situation" or saving life; (b) it was
-- accidental, from damage not caused "wilfully or recklessly", with "all reasonable precautions ... taken before and after"; (c) it
-- was "for the purpose of avoiding or minimising pollution incidents"; (d) it "occurred on the high seas, and comprised the same
-- ballast water and sediments that had been taken up in the high seas"; or (e) it was "at the same location where the whole of the
-- discharged ballast water or sediments originated" and unmixed with unmanaged water from elsewhere.
-- s 26(1): "This Act does not apply to any warship, naval auxiliary or other ship owned or operated by a State (including the
-- Government) and used for the time being, only on government non-commercial service."
--
-- One flag stands for the "reasonable precautions" in each provision; s 10B(b) asks for them before and after, the others after.
-- Exceptions (ss 6(2), 7(2), 10(2), 10A(2)) and the s 10B defence, which the accused must prove, are treated alike as defeating
-- the offence.
DECLARE `Ship section` IS ONE OF
    `section 6`
    `section 7`
    `section 10`
    `section 10A`
    `no discharge offence in the Act`

GIVEN `the pollutant` IS A Pollutant
GIVETH A `Ship section`
`the ship discharge section` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the pollutant`
    WHEN `oil` THEN `section 7`
    WHEN `an oily mixture` THEN `section 7`
    WHEN `refuse` THEN `section 6`
    WHEN `garbage` THEN `section 6`
    WHEN `plastics` THEN `section 6`
    WHEN `waste matter` THEN `section 6`
    WHEN `trade effluent` THEN `section 6`
    WHEN `a marine pollutant in packaged form` THEN `section 6`
    WHEN `a noxious liquid substance` THEN `section 10`
    WHEN `sediments` THEN `section 10A`
    WHEN `ballast water` THEN `section 10A`
    OTHERWISE `no discharge offence in the Act`

DECLARE `Ship discharge` HAS
    `the substance` IS A Pollutant
    `from a Singapore ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `into Singapore waters` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carried as cargo in bulk` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on government non-commercial service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `necessary for ship safety or saving life` IS A BOOLEAN
    `escaped through damage to the ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `damage was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable precautions were taken` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved to combat a pollution incident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a synthetic fishing net lost despite precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ballast water management under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to avoid or minimise pollution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `high-seas ballast discharged on the high seas` IS A BOOLEAN
    `discharged where it originated, unmixed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the discharge` IS A `Ship discharge`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discharge is within reach` IF
    CONSIDER `the ship discharge section` (`the discharge`'s `the substance`)
    WHEN `section 6` THEN `the discharge`'s `into Singapore waters`
    WHEN `section 7` THEN `the discharge`'s `into Singapore waters` OR `the discharge`'s `from a Singapore ship`
    WHEN `section 10` THEN `the discharge`'s `carried as cargo in bulk`
                           AND (`the discharge`'s `into Singapore waters` OR `the discharge`'s `from a Singapore ship`)
    WHEN `section 10A` THEN `the discharge`'s `into Singapore waters` OR `the discharge`'s `from a Singapore ship`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the discharge` IS A `Ship discharge`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the escape through damage is excused` IF
        `the discharge`'s `escaped through damage to the ship`
    AND (NOT `the discharge`'s `damage was intentional or reckless`)
    AND `the discharge`'s `reasonable precautions were taken`

GIVEN `the discharge` IS A `Ship discharge`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discharge is excepted or defended` IF
    CONSIDER `the ship discharge section` (`the discharge`'s `the substance`)
    WHEN `section 6` THEN `the discharge`'s `necessary for ship safety or saving life`
                          OR `the escape through damage is excused` `the discharge`
                          OR `the discharge`'s `a synthetic fishing net lost despite precautions`
    WHEN `section 7` THEN `the discharge`'s `necessary for ship safety or saving life`
                          OR `the escape through damage is excused` `the discharge`
                          OR (`the discharge`'s `approved to combat a pollution incident`
                              AND `the discharge`'s `the substance` EQUALS `an oily mixture`)
    WHEN `section 10` THEN `the discharge`'s `necessary for ship safety or saving life`
                           OR `the escape through damage is excused` `the discharge`
                           OR `the discharge`'s `approved to combat a pollution incident`
    WHEN `section 10A` THEN `the discharge`'s `ballast water management under the regulations`
                            OR `the discharge`'s `necessary for ship safety or saving life`
                            OR `the escape through damage is excused` `the discharge`
                            OR `the discharge`'s `to avoid or minimise pollution`
                            OR `the discharge`'s `high-seas ballast discharged on the high seas`
                            OR `the discharge`'s `discharged where it originated, unmixed`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the discharge` IS A `Ship discharge`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the master, owner and agent each commit an offence` IF
        (NOT `the discharge`'s `on government non-commercial service`)
    AND `the discharge is within reach` `the discharge`
    AND (NOT `the discharge is excepted or defended` `the discharge`)

§§ `2(1) "master" -- who answers for a ship's discharge`

-- ss 6(1), 7(1), 10(1), 10A(1): "the master, the owner and the agent of the ship shall each be guilty of an offence". s 2(1):
-- "master" includes every person, "except a pilot", having command or charge of any ship. (s 10A(4) widens "owner" to a manager or
-- bareboat charterer who has taken over the ISM Code duties; s 8 names only the master and owner.)
DECLARE `Ship role` IS ONE OF
    `the master`
    `the owner`
    `the agent`
    `a pilot in charge of the ship`
    `a crew member`

GIVEN `the role` IS A `Ship role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the role answers for the ship's discharge` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `the master` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the owner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the agent` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `15 -- reporting a ship's discharge`

-- s 15(1): on "any actual or probable discharge of any harmful substance ... in prescribed circumstances" from a Singapore ship
-- anywhere or any ship into Singapore waters, "the master of the ship must without delay report the occurrence". (2): a defence if
-- the master "was unable to comply". (3): where the master is unable, or the ship is abandoned, "the owner, charterer, manager and
-- operator of the ship or an agent" must report. (4): $5,000. (5): for (3), a defence if the person proves (a) "that the person was
-- not aware of the relevant occurrence"; or (b) where (3)(a) applies, "that the person neither knew nor suspected that the master
-- ... was unable to comply".
-- (s 16, not encoded: from land or an apparatus, the occupier or person in charge must "forthwith" report to the Port Master;
-- $5,000.)
GIVEN `a reportable discharge occurred` IS A BOOLEAN, `the master reported without delay` IS A BOOLEAN, `the master was unable to report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the master commits a reporting offence` IF
    `a reportable discharge occurred` AND (NOT `the master reported without delay`) AND (NOT `the master was unable to report`)

DECLARE `Owner's position` HAS
    `master was unable to report` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ship was abandoned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `owner reported without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
    `owner was not aware of the occurrence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `owner neither knew nor suspected the master was unable` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the position` IS AN `Owner's position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner commits a reporting offence` IF
        (`the position`'s `master was unable to report` OR `the position`'s `ship was abandoned`)
    AND (NOT `the position`'s `owner reported without delay`)
    AND (NOT `the position`'s `owner was not aware of the occurrence`)
    AND (NOT (`the position`'s `master was unable to report` AND `the position`'s `owner neither knew nor suspected the master was unable`))

§§ `17 and 18 -- the ship owner pays for the clean-up`

-- s 17(1): if refuse, garbage, waste matter, plastics, marine pollutant in packaged form or trade effluent "is discharged from any
-- ship into Singapore waters or into any part of the sea or waters outside Singapore waters and ... subsequently drifts or flows into
-- Singapore waters, the owner of the ship shall be liable to pay for the costs of any measure reasonably taken by the appointed
-- authority". s 18(1): the same for oil, oily mixture or noxious liquid substance. (2) of each: owners of 2 or more ships are jointly
-- and severally liable where the costs "cannot reasonably be separated". s 18(4): s 18 does not apply to oil or oily mixture where
-- s 3 of the Merchant Shipping (Civil Liability and Compensation for Oil Pollution) Act 1998 applies, nor to bunker oil where s 3 of
-- the bunker oil Act 2008 applies. s 21: the costs are "recoverable ... as a debt". (Neither section names carcases, sediments or
-- ballast water.)
GIVEN `the pollutant` IS A Pollutant,
      `discharged into Singapore waters` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `drifted into Singapore waters` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a civil liability Act for oil applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ship owner must pay the removal costs` IF
        (`discharged into Singapore waters` OR `drifted into Singapore waters`)
    AND CONSIDER `the ship discharge section` `the pollutant`
        WHEN `section 6` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `section 7` THEN NOT `a civil liability Act for oil applies`
        WHEN `section 10` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Penalties -- selected offences`

-- s 3 and s 7: "not less than $1,000 and not more than $1 million" or up to 2 years. s 5: up to $20,000 or 6 months. s 8: master and
-- owner each "a fine not exceeding $1 million" (no imprisonment). s 14(3): a knowingly false or misleading record-book entry, up to
-- $10,000 or 12 months. s 15(4): $5,000. s 22(3): obstructing or lying to an inspector, up to $5,000 or 6 months. s 24(1): a
-- detained ship proceeding to sea, up to $10,000 or 2 years. Imprisonment of 0 means the provision gives none.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `oil from land or apparatus (s 3)`
    `throwing pollutants (s 5)`
    `oil from a ship (s 7)`
    `not retaining oil residues (s 8)`
    `false record-book entry (s 14(3))`
    `failing to report a ship discharge (s 15)`
    `obstructing an inspector (s 22(3))`
    `detained ship proceeding to sea (s 24(1))`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `oil from land or apparatus (s 3)` THEN 1000000
    WHEN `throwing pollutants (s 5)` THEN 20000
    WHEN `oil from a ship (s 7)` THEN 1000000
    WHEN `not retaining oil residues (s 8)` THEN 1000000
    WHEN `false record-book entry (s 14(3))` THEN 10000
    WHEN `failing to report a ship discharge (s 15)` THEN 5000
    WHEN `obstructing an inspector (s 22(3))` THEN 5000
    WHEN `detained ship proceeding to sea (s 24(1))` THEN 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `oil from land or apparatus (s 3)` THEN 1000
    WHEN `oil from a ship (s 7)` THEN 1000
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `oil from land or apparatus (s 3)` THEN 24
    WHEN `throwing pollutants (s 5)` THEN 6
    WHEN `oil from a ship (s 7)` THEN 24
    WHEN `false record-book entry (s 14(3))` THEN 12
    WHEN `obstructing an inspector (s 22(3))` THEN 6
    WHEN `detained ship proceeding to sea (s 24(1))` THEN 24
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `11(6) -- ignoring a reception-facility direction`

-- s 11(6): failing to comply with a Minister's direction under s 11(4) or (5) within the period: "a fine not exceeding $10,000 and,
-- in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $100 for every day during which the offence continues after
-- conviction".
GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for ignoring a direction` MEANS
    10000 PLUS 100 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

§§ `33 -- composition`

-- s 33(1): the Director, Port Master or an authorised person "may compound any offence ... which is prescribed as a compoundable
-- offence, by collecting ... a sum not exceeding $2,000".
GIVEN `the sum` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for the sum` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable` AND `the sum` AT MOST 2000
